NOTES, WHICH ARE NOT CONDITIONS

Images and video you make with this camera are yours. This licence covers the
software only and claims no interest whatsoever in your photographs, footage,
or anything you produce with it. Sell them, print them, exhibit them.

The source is public so that the claims made on the site can be checked. There
is no server, no upload, and no analytics; the camera feed is processed in your
browser and discarded. Read the code and confirm it.

The underlying ideas are not claimed and are not claimable. The allRGB
constraint predates this work by well over a decade and belongs to the
community that built it. Space-filling curves through colour space are older
still, and the 3D Hilbert construction follows Skilling's algorithm. What is
licensed here is this particular implementation, not the concepts behind it.

Want to use this commercially — running your own hosted version, bundling it
into a product, or anything else outside personal/noncommercial use? Get in
touch rather than assuming; that's the one thing this licence, unlike MIT,
doesn't hand out for free.
